<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Leon Trotsky</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1879">1879</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lev Bronstein</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Leon Trotsky was a Russian Marxist revolutionary who organised the Bolshevik seizure of power in October 1917 with Lenin. As People's Commissar for War from 1918 he built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> and led it to victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-civil-war">Russian Civil War</a>. Defeated by Stalin in the struggle for power, he was expelled from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in 1929 and murdered by a Soviet agent in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1940.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/leon-trotsky.jpg" alt="Leon Trotsky" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rijksmuseum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Leon_Trotsky_1918_(3x4_rotated_cropped_b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
